      "body": "Fixes #48401.\n\nHybrid Mamba2 models (like NemotronH) raise the cache block size to match the mamba layout (8320 tokens here). Prefix caching only records a full block, so when `max_model_len` is smaller than the block size, no request can ever fill a block and the cache never hits. Prefix caching does nothing, with no warning.\n\nEvidence (same model and GPU, only max_model_len differs):\n- max_model_len 4096 (< block size 8320): prefix_cache_hits = 0 out of 10608 queries.\n- max_model_len 16384 (> block size 8320): hits = 16640 out of 38448 (~43%).\n\nSo prefix caching is inert whenever block_size > max_model_len. This PR adds a warning at startup for that case. One warning, no behavior change.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
